            <history xml:id="history_307f6b52">
               <p xml:id="idm77">In July 1850 Carsten Hauch asked Gade, if he would compose the music for his new comedy "Flugten til Sæteren" which comprised some twenty-two songs. In the autumn the manuscript was handed in to the Royal Theatre but rejected. At that time Gade apparently had only completed the overture, later published with the German title "Nordische Sennfahrt" (NWGW 15), and had made sketches for some of the songs.</p>
            </history>
